# The blog is built by .github/workflows/deploy-pages.yml from blog-src/.
# It used to be committed pre-built; keeping both would mean two sources of truth, and the
# committed copy would be the one that quietly went stale.
/blog/
/_site/

# Hugo build artifacts
/blog-src/public/
/blog-src/resources/
/blog-src/.hugo_build.lock

# Unpublished drafts stay out of this PUBLIC repo.
# Hugo does not build a `draft: true` post, so it would never reach the site — but its
# markdown would still be readable by anyone on GitHub. The old pre-built setup kept drafts
# out as a side effect of only ever committing built HTML; now that the source lives here,
# that has to be deliberate. Drop the line below when the post is ready to go live.
/blog-src/content/posts/thesis-from-papers/
